; Verify one tape block of SAVE
;
; Compares a block on tape with memory through the ROM's LD-BYTES (carry clear on
; entry means verify). Called by #R$84CC for each of the four state blocks, with
; the block address in IX, its length in DE and the flag byte in A. When the
; block is right returns to SaveGame. When it differs prints "Tape error -
; hit any key to continue.", waits for a key and ends the SAVE command at
; #R$8553: the POP DE drops the return address into SaveGame, so the command
; ends here.
; .
; Hardware: the ROM tape routine (LD-BYTES; it returns with interrupts on); the
; keyboard port $FE.
;
; A Flag byte of the block
; F Carry clear: verify
; IX Address of the block
; DE Length of the block
@label=VerifyBlock
c$855A CALL $0556           ; ROM LD-BYTES, verify
 $855D RET C                ; carry set: the block matched
@isub=LD A,1
 $855E LD A,$01             ; RawOutputFlag: input window
@isub=LD (RawOutputFlag),A
 $8560 LD ($B701),A
 $8563 LD HL,$B381          ; "Tape error - hit any key to continue."
 $8566 CALL $72DD
@label=VerifyBlock_Wait
*$8569 XOR A                ; A = 0 selects every half-row
@isub=IN A,(PORT_ULA)
 $856A IN A,($FE)
@isub=AND KEY_BITS
 $856C AND $1F
@isub=CP KEY_BITS
 $856E CP $1F
 $8570 JR Z,$8569
 $8572 POP DE               ; drop the return address
 $8573 JP $8553             ; SaveGame_End: end the command
